{"type":"FeatureCollection","features":[{"type":"Feature","properties":{"place":"chong-kara","region":"KG","donors":"UZ","rank":3,"whose_line":"OSM mappers: the Chong-Kara (Chon-Qora) exclave as drawn in Uzbekistan's So'x District before its transfer","publisher":"OpenStreetMap contributors","source_url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/relation/3772474","version_or_date":"snapshot 2026-10-04T06:57:51Z (Overpass attic query); relation 3772474 v29 (2026-07-18T05:56:45Z)","feature_id":"relation 3772474 (the part at 71.0375, 40.2508)","licence":"ODbL 1.0","notes":"Not a dispute: an agreed transfer (R054) neither GADM 4.1 nor OSM (as of the snapshot) shows. 'два населенных пункта — Чонгара и Таш-Тобо — перешли в состав Кыргызской Республики' (24.kg, 2026-06-23, quoting the presidential press secretary, https://24.kg/vlast/379159_kyirgyizstan_iuzbekistan_obmenyalis_selami_chto_budet_sjitelyami/, read 2026-10-05); the basis is the border treaty signed in November 2022 (same article). That the whole exclave as OSM draws it was transferred is not stated in so many words. Tash-Tobo (Jangail) needs no geometry: GADM already puts its point (40.2008, 71.6694) in Kyrgyzstan's Kadamjai unit, while OSM still draws it as Uzbek.","input_sha256":"b7405303d6fc47ea8e9a79f39923af7eb8ac238ccb537ae0d6b7481c3046cbe2","operation":"assembled from the OSM element's member ways (outer minus inner); only the parts that contain the points [[71.0375, 40.2508]]","crs":"WGS84 longitude/latitude, as in the source (no reprojection)","source_features":[{"id":"relation 3772474 v29","osm":"relation/3772474","version":29,"timestamp":"2026-07-18T05:56:45Z","name":"Soʻx tumani","name:en":"So'x District","boundary":"administrative","admin_level":"6"}]},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[71.0298831,40.2348244],[71.029183,40.235109],[71.028152,40.2356559],[71.0275947,40.2362995],[71.0272244,40.2368474],[71.0267441,40.2375192],[71.0261722,40.2380061],[71.0257751,40.238863],[71.0251445,40.2395567],[71.